event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0e23e494d06f8e78006ad5e8c9f38c87d2a5059d28e16cf7dc","logprobs":[],"output_index":0,"sequence_number":360,"text":"**Travel and Expenses Policy v2.0 — hotels**\n\n- **Nightly maximums per person:** London £200; rest of the UK £130; Lisbon or Dublin €180; other EU cities €160. Outside the UK, convert costs at the rate on the day incurred. These are maximums, not allowances. (Section 4, p. 2)\n- **Booking and approval:** Book hotels through the intranet travel portal, which applies the limits and sends bookings to your line manager for approval. Book at least 14 days ahead where possible. A last-minute booking over the limit needs written head-of-department approval. Outside-portal bookings are reimbursable only if the portal could not offer a comparable option; explain why in the claim. (Section 3, p. 1)\n- **What the limit covers:** Room and taxes. It excludes minibar, room service beyond the meals limit, films, laundry for stays under five nights, and late checkout. For stays spanning a policy change, each night is paid at the limit in force that night. (Section 4.2, p. 2)\n- **Alternative and exceptions:** If staying with friends or family instead of a hotel, you may claim £25 per night toward a thank-you gift or meal, with a receipt. Self-booked hotel upgrades are not reimbursed. (Sections 4.2 and 8, p. 2–3)\n- **Claims:** Every claim needs line-manager approval; claims over £500 also need head-of-department approval, and those over £2,000 also need CFO approval. Keep an itemised receipt for each expense above £25. (Sections 5 and 7, p. 2–3)"}

