event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_025d3a57ed5a88e4006ad5e8cad8f087d29b5e0e17e1f1d1e7","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":334,"text":"**Travel and Expenses Policy, version 1.0** (effective 1 January 2025):\n\n- **Nightly limits, per person:** London £180; rest of the UK £120; Lisbon or Dublin €170; other EU cities €150. Non-UK costs are converted at the rate on the day incurred. (Section 4, p. 2)\n- **Booking and approval:** Book hotels through the travel booking portal; it applies the limits and sends the booking to your line manager for approval. Bookings outside the portal are reimbursable only if it could not offer a comparable option, and you must explain why in the claim. Book at least 14 days ahead where possible. Last-minute bookings over the limit need written approval from your head of department. (Section 3, p. 1)\n- **What the limit covers and exceptions:** The nightly limit covers the room and taxes, but not minibar, room service beyond the meals limit, films, laundry for stays under five nights, or late checkout. If you stay with friends or family instead, you may claim £25 per night toward a thank-you gift or meal, with a receipt. (Section 4.2, p. 2)\n- **Other relevant rules:** Self-booked hotel upgrades are not reimbursed. Keep an itemised receipt for a single expense over £50. Every claim needs line-manager approval; claims over £500 also need head-of-department approval, and over £2,000 also need CFO approval. (Sections 5, 7 and 8, pp. 2–3)"}

